# CLI reference

The `pontia` CLI configures the local installation and delegates durable control-plane operations to the running `pontiad` service.

Use `pontia COMMAND --help` for the exact options in your installed version.

## Setup and lifecycle

| Command | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `pontia init` | Select Agent Clients, create persistent configuration, install integrations, start the per-user service, and offer remote setup |
| `pontia up` | Install or refresh the per-user service definition and start or restart the service |
| `pontia status` | Show installation, enabled, running, and HTTP health state |
| `pontia down` | Stop and disable the per-user service |
| `pontia update` | Install the latest signed stable `pontia` and `pontiad` release |
| `pontia --version` | Print the installed version |

See [Initialization](/docs/initialization) for interactive setup and the equivalent step-by-step command sequence.

Stopping `pontiad` stops observation, input reception, and Workflow scheduling. Agent Clients manage the lifecycle of their native conversations separately.

## Cloud login and remote access

| Command | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `pontia login` | Complete browser-based device authorization and store a CLI credential |
| `pontia remote edges` | List available edges as a JSON array of IDs and names |
| `pontia remote enable` | Register this device, select an edge interactively, and create its E2E identity |
| `pontia remote enable --edge EDGE_ID --name NAME` | Register without prompts; both options are required |
| `pontia remote status` | Compare local identity state with the Cloud registration |
| `pontia remote edit --name NAME` | Change the device display name |
| `pontia remote edit --handle HANDLE` | Change the device Dashboard URL handle |
| `pontia remote rotate-key` | Replace the device E2E identity and key version |
| `pontia remote disable` | Unregister this device and remove its local remote identity |

Remote configuration changes that affect `pontiad` restart the local service automatically.

## Workflows

| Command | Context | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `pontia workflow run FILE` | Any local shell | Parse a TOML definition and start a Workflow through the local API |
| `pontia workflow show [WORKFLOW_ID]` | Any local shell; ID optional inside a managed Node | Print compact Workflow, current Node, input, output, and Patch context |
| `pontia workflow submit` | Current managed Agent Node pane | Declare the Node's output ready |
| `pontia workflow patch request` | Current managed Agent Node pane | Report a blocking problem and start replanning |
| `pontia workflow patch apply` | Current Re-planner pane | Accept the candidate definition as a new revision |
| `pontia workflow patch block` | Current Re-planner pane | Finish the Patch without applying the candidate definition |

Run pane-scoped commands in the current Agent Node or Re-planner's Pontia-managed `tmux` pane.

## Exit status and errors

Use the exit status to check command success. Errors are written to standard error with a `pontia:` prefix. Include the redacted error when diagnosing a failure.

## `pontia-edge`

A self-hosted Edge has a separate root-operated CLI:

| Command | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `pontia-edge init --edge-id ID --ticket TICKET` | Initialize and register an Edge; normally use the full Cloud-generated command |
| `pontia-edge retry` | Resume incomplete initialization on the same server |
| `pontia-edge update` | Install the latest signed stable Edge release |
| `pontia-edge auto-update enable` | Install and enable hourly update checks |
| `pontia-edge auto-update disable` | Disable future checks |
| `pontia-edge auto-update status` | Show timer schedule and the last update result |

See [Self-host an Edge](/docs/self-hosted-edge) before using these commands directly.
